  message: "## Wave 4 progress + Cluster F cross-cluster note (audit-findings 0011)\n\nWI-mihiz closed (PR #3569 merged). Wave 4 status: 3/4 done (WI-rusit, WI-zarov, WI-mihiz); WI-nibis remains.\n\n**Cross-cluster note for Wave 6 schedulers:** audit-findings 0011 (Symbol.kind Cluster F, just landed) intentionally does NOT file a verdict row for `component_file`. That value's verdict is governed by audit-findings 0005 (Cluster B file-shape) where it sits as `verdict: FOLD, fold_target: file, status: PRELIM_RESOLVED` with rationale \"Vue / Svelte / Astro single-file component. Structurally a kind=file with framework metadata. Fold to file + meta['component_framework']='vue' (or 'svelte', etc.).\"\n\nWhen Wave 6 (per this WI's schedule: \"fold gajob/dubab to canonical OR land their new axis ADRs\") executes the Cluster B producer migration, the `component_file` rows in audit-findings 0005 are the canonical reference — audit-findings 0011 §\"Diagnostic findings #4\" pins the cross-doc relationship. The vue_component linker (linkers/vue_component.py) is the lone producer of `component_file` Symbols; its fold target is `kind='file'` + `meta['component_framework']='vue'`. Astro and Svelte have no component_file producer today (only the Vue linker emits the file-Symbol shape).\n\nThis note exists because the Cluster F audit's PR-scope drop of `component_ref` would otherwise leave a Wave-6 reader asking \"what about component_file?\" without a clear pointer back to 0005."  # 73e5
