  nonce: '2827'  # 2827
  message: "## Wave 5 COMPLETE\n\nWave 5 of the cross-axis schedule (framework-dispatch coordinated fold) shipped 6 PRs across this session:\n\n- **PR #1** (Codeberg #3572): websocket / tauri / grpc / openapi producer fold — 4 framework_role kinds + ~8 framework_dispatch evidence_types\n- **PR #2** (selfh #162, failover engaged): graphql / http / crypto / ipc / objc — ~9 framework_role + ~7 framework_dispatch\n- **PR #3** (selfh #163): event-dispatch / yjs / message_dispatch / annotation_convention / Go-route_mount — ~5 framework_role + ~5 framework_dispatch\n- **PR #4** (selfh #164): Ruby / Django framework_dispatch — 10 evidence_types across 5 producer files\n- **PR #5** (selfh #165): single-row dispatch modules batched — 27 evidence_types across 25 producers, including pattern-shape detection_pattern fold (6 rows: abi_name, jni_naming, phoenix_event, implicit_convention, table_name, subprocess_cli)\n- **PR #6** (selfh #166): Symbol.kind=route sweep — the highest-blast-radius value: 17 src producer files, 14 production consumers, ~330 sites total. framework_patterns.py Pattern.matches() extended to fall back to meta.framework_role for backward-compat with existing YAML rules.\n\nTotal scope: ~75 evidence_type values + ~28 Symbol.kind values folded across Cluster C and Cluster D per audit-findings 0013/0014. WI-habut and WI-kagik can move to PRELIM_RESOLVED on the producer-side migration completion (Phase 4a deprecation window applies; Phase 4b cleanup after bakeoff validation).\n\n**Failover state:** PRs #2-#6 (selfh #162-166) await disengage repatriation when Codeberg's PR-creation API recovers (was returning HTTP 500 on both AGit-style push and REST POST /pulls at session start). PR #1 (#3572) shipped to Codeberg before failover engaged.\n\nWave 6 next per the schedule: Cluster B producer migration (component_file fold per audit-findings 0011 cross-cluster note + Wave 6 Cluster H registry cleanup pruning of DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD vocabulary). WI-rusit (Cluster C apex/peer fold) is also still outstanding from Wave 4, though it's now Wave 5.5 / 6.5 territory per the existing schedule discussion."  # 2827
- op: discuss  # 7ee3
  at: '2026-05-11T19:44:34Z'  # 7ee3
  by: agent  # 7ee3
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7ee3
  clock: 11  # 7ee3
  nonce: 7ee3  # 7ee3
  message: "## Wave 6 + Wave 7 COMPLETE; Symbol.is_resolved ADR WITHDRAWN\n\nUpdating the living-document schedule to reflect closure since the 2026-05-06T13:37:44Z entry.\n\n### Wave 6 — Cluster B/G/H follow-through: COMPLETE\nSix PRs landed (commits 3f9b2507f7, f56d8ac95c, 69315269c4, e127932c08, 2d807d2ddd, ac7b561d50):\n- WI-gajob Wave 6 PR 1 + PR 3 — Cluster B canonical promotions + FOLDs\n- WI-dubab/WI-nupus Wave 6 PR 2 — Clusters G+H canonical promotions\n- WI-runod Wave 6 PR 4 — Cluster G/H DEPRECATE-NO-FOLDs + theorem/inductive/message reclassification\n- WI-dubab Wave 6 PR 5 — Cluster G FOLDs\n- WI-runod Wave 6 PR 6 — Cluster H boundary-pseudo-symbol resolution\n\n### Wave 5.5/6.5 — Symbol.is_resolved parallel ADR: WITHDRAWN\nThe proposed ADR (filed as a possibility in the 2026-05-05T06:58:40Z entry) was investigated end-to-end during Wave 6 PR 6's re-trace and found NOT WARRANTED:\n\n1. `Symbol(kind='unresolved')` has no producer — the 'unresolved' string appears only as a trailing token in dangling-edge dst IDs (analyze/base.py::make_unresolved_call_edge), and that resolution-status attribute is already captured by `Edge.is_resolved=False` per ADR-0028.\n2. The IR boundary materializer always emits `kind='external_symbol'` regardless of `_parse_dangling_id` output.\n3. No consumer reads `Symbol.kind == 'external_symbol'` as a discriminator — boundary status flows through `is_external_boundary(sym)` which reads `meta['external_boundary']=True`.\n4. ADR-0024's fold-residue threshold for promoting a meta key to a sibling field (≥3 distinct values OR ≥2 producer modules) is NOT met: 1 producer, 0 consumer reads, 0 paired-suffix variants. vs ADR-0028's threshold-met case: 10 paired *_resolved/*_unresolved evidence types across 4+ producer modules.\n\nResolution: `external_symbol` promoted DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD → CANONICAL/RESOLVED. ADR-0027 Phase 3 producer migration is now empirically complete on Symbol.kind: every value in the registry has a verdict and a status of RESOLVED or PRELIM_RESOLVED.\n\n### Wave 7 — Phase 4a deprecation marks: COMPLETE\nBoth axes shipped in commit bf34b47aa2 (feat(schema): Phase 4a x-deprecated for Symbol.kind and Edge.evidence_type — WI-tikuh + WI-jubak). Tracker status updated this session — was stale.\n\n### BVT validation state for Phase 3 clusters\n- evidence_type Cluster B (WI-nunal): MOVED, cohorts 1+2 (2026-05-11). Auto-stripped.\n- evidence_type Cluster D (WI-nibis): MOVED, cohorts 1+2 (2026-05-11). Auto-stripped.\n- Symbol.kind Clusters D/E/F + evidence_type Cluster C (WI-habut, WI-zarov, WI-mihiz, WI-kagik): tags applied 2026-05-07, no longer in BVT queue → silently stripped.\n- Symbol.kind Cluster C (WI-rusit): no quantitative claim at merge (producer fold already in place); tag not applied per BVT discipline. Status updated done this session.\n- Symbol.kind Clusters B/G/H (Wave 6): tag-state unverified — six PRs landed between 2026-05-06 and the BVT-aggregate run on 2026-05-11. Likely auto-stripped during that aggregate cycle but not individually confirmed here.\n\n### What remains: Wave 8 + Wave 9\nWave 8 (WI-butol Symbol.kind 4b + WI-porim evidence_type 4b) is unblocked for the six BVT-cleared clusters (Symbol.kind D, E, F + evidence_type B, C, D). Can ship per-cluster removal PRs immediately. Wave 6 cluster (B/G/H) 4b removal pending tag-state verification.\n\nWave 9 (WI-vusot — axis_meta_keys.py parallel registry) is unblocked; the isbefore edges from WI-habut and WI-kagik are satisfied.\n\nWave 2 leftover: WI-jukav slice 2 (containment.CONTAINABLE/CONTAINER + EXCLUDED_KINDS) is unblocked now that Wave 5 framework-role fold completed. Still `todo_soft` P3.\n\n### Schedule status snapshot\nWaves 0-7 complete. Wave 5.5/6.5 (Symbol.is_resolved) withdrawn after investigation. Waves 8-9 ready to ship."  # 7ee3
- op: discuss  # 59c0
