  clock: 12  # 59c0
  nonce: 59c0  # 59c0
  message: "## Correction to prior entry: Wave 6 Cluster H is not pending tag-state verification\n\nThe prior entry said 'Symbol.kind Clusters B/G/H (Wave 6): tag-state unverified ... not individually confirmed here.' On re-check that caveat is wrong:\n\n- **Cluster B (WI-gajob)**: MOVED on re-audit at the correct surface (2026-05-11T04:33:06Z). Tag stripped. Wave 6 PR 3 (selfh #181) was the producer migration; the re-audit script confirmed 0 nodes carrying any of the 11 disputed Cluster B kinds across all 12 cohort hg.json files.\n- **Cluster G (WI-dubab)**: MOVED on re-audit at the correct surface (2026-05-11T04:33:07Z). Tag stripped. Wave 6 PR 5 (selfh #183) was the producer migration; same shape of re-audit confirmed 0 nodes carrying 9 disputed Cluster G kinds.\n- **Cluster H (WI-nupus / WI-runod PR 4 + PR 6)**: never tagged, correctly. The Wave 6 PR 2 canonical promotions are additive (no vocabulary going off the wire); the Wave 6 PR 4 DEPRECATE-NO-FOLDs target dead vocabulary with no producer to migrate (per commit body: 'no producer for heading', 'ID-string-only synthetic at prisma.py:120'); the Wave 6 PR 6 boundary-pseudo work is a registry-only reclassification (`external_symbol` is 'a label not a load-bearing classifier' per commit body). No producer vocabulary changes shipped → no quantitative BVT trigger per the bakeoff-validation-tagging-discipline playbook.\n\n**Net: Wave 8 is fully unblocked across all clusters.** WI-butol and WI-porim can ship per-cluster 4b removal PRs immediately for every Phase 3 cluster (Symbol.kind C, D, E, F, B, G + evidence_type B, C, D)."  # 59c0
