  message: "## Underlying program COMPLETE (Waves 0-9 all shipped)\n\nFinal session update.\n\n### This session's PRs\n| # | Commit | Subject |\n|---|---|---|\n| #3632 | 77a6a896d6 | feat(axis): axis_meta_keys.py parallel registry (ADR-0024 Wave 9) |\n| (auto-sync) | 4892756f22 | tracker: sync (WI-tikuh/WI-jubak/WI-rusit closures + this thread) |\n| #3633 | c59dbd8160 | refactor(symbol_kinds): ADR-0027 §6 Phase 4b — Symbol.kind enum closure |\n| (auto-sync) | (WI-butol close) | tracker: sync |\n| #3635 | 0a3b70fbc4 | refactor(evidence_types): ADR-0028 §6 Phase 4b — Edge.evidence_type enum closure |\n\n### Wave-by-wave final status\n- **Wave 0** (housekeeping) — complete (prior sessions).\n- **Wave 1** (canonical audit docs) — complete (prior sessions).\n- **Wave 2** (consumer migrations) — complete. WI-fukol done; WI-jukav slice 1 + slice 2 both done. Slice 2 closed this session as verification-only (the dual-predicate work already shipped in slice 1; CONTAINABLE/CONTAINER carry audit verdicts; other hardcoded sets are intentional curated vocabularies).\n- **Wave 3** (canary producer fold WI-nunal) — complete (prior session).\n- **Wave 4** (mid-scale folds) — complete. WI-rusit closed this session (Cluster C apex/peer registry classification shipped in commit c968aebf2c earlier; tracker state was stale).\n- **Wave 5** (framework-dispatch coordinated pair WI-habut + WI-kagik) — complete (6 PRs prior session).\n- **Wave 5.5 / 6.5** (Symbol.is_resolved sibling ADR) — WITHDRAWN. Wave 6 PR 6 re-trace found no leak to absorb; ADR-0024 §'Fold-residue discipline' rule 3 threshold not met (1 producer, 0 consumer reads, 0 paired-suffix variants). external_symbol promoted DEPRECATE-NO-FOLD → CANONICAL/RESOLVED.\n- **Wave 6** (Cluster B/G/H follow-through) — complete (6 PRs prior session: 3f9b2507f7 / f56d8ac95c / 69315269c4 / e127932c08 / 2d807d2ddd / ac7b561d50).\n- **Wave 7** (Phase 4a deprecation marks) — complete. WI-tikuh + WI-jubak closed this session (shipped via commit bf34b47aa2 earlier; tracker state was stale).\n- **Wave 8** (Phase 4b enum closure) — complete this session. WI-butol shipped PR #3633 (71 Symbol.kind endpoint_shape values removed, SCHEMA_VERSION 0.5.8 → 0.6.0). WI-porim shipped PR #3635 (111 Edge.evidence_type endpoint_shape values removed, SCHEMA_VERSION 0.6.0 → 0.7.0). 163 audit-findings rows advanced PRELIM_RESOLVED → RESOLVED across 10 docs (0005-0011, 0013 on Symbol.kind; 0008, 0012, 0014 on Edge.evidence_type).\n- **Wave 9** (axis_meta_keys parallel registry WI-vusot) — complete this session. PR #3632. 56 meta keys registered (17 Edge.meta + 39 Symbol.meta); 15 invariant + accessor tests at 100% coverage. Subscript-access drift linter deferred as a separate follow-on (the registry without the linter is already useful as the canonical vocabulary).\n\n### Schema version trajectory\n- Wave 8 Symbol.kind:  0.5.8 → 0.6.0\n- Wave 8 evidence_type: 0.6.0 → 0.7.0\n- Net for this session: 0.5.8 → 0.7.0 (two minor bumps, hard-contract changes)\n\n### Registry size impact (post-session)\n- Symbol.kind:    208 → 137 entries (71 endpoint_shape removed)\n- Edge.evidence_type: 228 → 117 entries (111 endpoint_shape removed)\n- axis_meta_keys: 0 → 56 entries (new registry seeded)\n\n### Living-document status\nPer the 2026-05-05T00:44 'living document' decision, WI-runod itself stays open as a perpetual cross-axis sequencing tracker. No further waves are scheduled; future updates land as discussion entries when new cross-axis sequencing decisions arise (e.g., the Open Question 2 `Edge.framework` field promotion if/when meta['framework_dispatch'] hits the recurrence threshold)."  # d4cf
